{"name":"Centaur Brown","hex":"#8b6a4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"centaur","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical beast having a horse's body with a man's head and torso in place of the head and neck of the horse.","One of a number of icy planetoids that orbit the Sun between Jupiter and Neptune."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/centaur"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Centaur","blocks":[{"text":"A centaur, occasionally hippocentaur, collectively called the Centaurs or the Ixionidae, is a creature from Greek mythology with the upper body of a human and the lower body and legs of a horse that was said to live in the mountains of Thessaly. In one version of the myth, the centaurs were named after Centaurus, and, through his brother Lapithes, were kin to the legendary tribe of the Lapiths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Terracotta_lekythos_%28oil_flask%29_with_centaur_battling_a_warrior_MET_DP161810.jpg/330px-Terracotta_lekythos_%28oil_flask%29_with_centaur_battling_a_warrior_MET_DP161810.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centaur","wikidata":"Q83203"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o